getbones() very carefully leaves the delete_bones() call until after
get_lev() has done its thing and all the resetobjs() tweaks have been
made; if loading the bones bails, the file should still be there.

(There are some preliminary checks made for the more obvious kind of
unusable bones, such as those belonging to an incompatible version, so
they can be disregarded without causing problems.)

The Hearse client, on the other hand, I don't know about.

